WEBVTT

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.040
Damn it!

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.990
What's going on here?!

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.710
Damn it!

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.820
Hey, why...

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.550
Why don't you give up already?!

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.510
Are you okay with being trapped here?!

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.720
Quiet down for a bit.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.820
I imagine Aria would be able to 
do something for us, though.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:07.480
She said something like, 
"Some of my power's returned!"

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.330
Do you think Aria's with the president?

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.650
Are you suggesting those two betrayed us?

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.980
Locking us up in this damn place!

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.660
We shouldn't talk like 
that behind their backs.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.970
But it's suspicious, isn't it?!

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.580
That's enough. Now calm 
down and figure out a plan—

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.130
How can I calm down?!

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.750
That's why we should all figure out a plan.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.790
Shut up!

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.610
This guy's impossible.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.410
What did you say?!

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.520
Stop!

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.750
That's enough.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.490
Hey, Shogo-sempai, please say something.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.220
He's in dire straits, too.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.180
But why would someone do this?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.900
I told you it's a trap!

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.770
There's a spy among us!

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.620
Would you be quiet!

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.850
I know you're upset how things
 ended up with Shadow Knife,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.860
but stop taking it out on us!

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.030
Er, sorry.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.230
Back then, Shadow Knife 
was waiting to ambush us.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.210
There wasn't anyone else 
at the Tower, either.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:09.500
It feels as if they knew everything 
we were going to do, right?

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.000
Huh? Me?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.720
Well, you're the one who 
brought us information, right?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.210
The spy has to be you, Kensuke-kun!

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.030
And what will you do to me if I am the spy?

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.770
Can we just stop those stupid conversations?

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.640
Quit screwing around, jerk!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:30.890
Stop it!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:38.860
Doubting each other like that 
isn't going to get us out of here.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.450
Ow.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.410
You're free to doubt me,

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:54.370
but I'm trapped in here as well,
 you know, Mr. Rescue Man.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.510
Stop it.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.260
If only Ritsu-sempai were here.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.410
Hey, Shogo-sempai,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.720
do you know where the 
president and Aria might be?

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.660
Can I ask you one thing?

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.150
Back at the Tower, when that 
Musician, Thorn, appeared...

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.320
What a pathetic man.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.740
What was that all about?

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.080
<i>You've known that girl for a while, right?</i>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.910
No way. Shogo, are you...

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.670
Hey, would you say something 
already, Shogo-sempai?!

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.000
Don't blame me!

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:43.160
Um, what's going on here, everyone?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.220
Who's there?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.180
U-Um, it's me.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.800
Marie-chan?

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.640
Yes.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.310
Hey! We've been trapped in here!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.870
Get us out of here!

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.230
Huh? You mean you didn't 
lock it from the inside?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.520
What do you mean?

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.480
It won't budge at all.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.010
What's going on here?

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:04.880
Damn.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.950
Um, do you know where Ritsu-sempai is?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.370
Huh? Shikishima-kun's not in there?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.800
No, that bastard...

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.660
I'm worried.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.850
Please! Find Ritsu for us!

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.750
All right.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.140
Oh, Marie-chan, hold on.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.590
She's gone.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.310
Marie-sempai still isn't back, is she?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.820
All because Kotaro-sempai sent her off

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.970
to search for the president without thinking.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:40.960
We might have been able to 
find some means of escape.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.280
We'll know for sure once she brings him back.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.240
During that battle a month ago,

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.070
it seemed as though the president and μ

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.850
had known each other for 
a long time, didn't it?

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:53.950
You're right.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.910
Maybe President was deceiving 
us from the very beginning.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.090
Maybe so.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:03.800
You're saying you can't trust our president?

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.260
No, that's not it.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.720
I'm saying I can't trust 
a single person here.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.680
I mean, that's how it is, right?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:19.480
We all lived trashy lives 
back in the real world,

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.450
and we came here to Mobius 
to escape from them.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.930
You can't trust us?

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.160
Not any of the friends you've made 
here in the Go-Home Club in Mobius?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.770
Can you?

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.810
Huh?

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.560
Ultimately, we've all just decided

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.410
that we want to run away 
from this place, too, right?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.430
You're getting too blunt there, you know.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.630
Sorry.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.630
But those are my honest feelings.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.090
Sh-Shogo-sempai...

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:51.050
Sempai, do you feel the same way?

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.180
Say something already, damn it!

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.820
Our past continues to 
haunt us, no matter we go.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.190
No matter how far we run...

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.710
No matter where we run to...

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.040
I...

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.250
I...

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.030
I can't escape it!

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.490
Not even in Mobius!

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.120
In the end both reality and Mobius are shit!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.380
I can't trust anything anymore!

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.790
It's just as Kashiwaba and Satake said.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.840
Ultimately, this is just

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.760
a gathering place for people who 
have suffered in the real world.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.720
We're all just being kept 
alive in this tepid bath

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.470
of whatever μ considers happiness.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.970
Yet even that's just a fabrication.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.440
Okay, why don't we do this?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:48.250
Before we start talking about 
trust or lack thereof,

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:52.000
we really don't know anything 
about each other at all, do we?

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.410
So why don't we go ahead and 
introduce ourselves again?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.120
Introduce ourselves?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.400
Yes. I'm incredibly 
interested in the reasons

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.770
you all decided to come here.

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.370
And it's a perfect way to kill time, right?

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.960
If that helps us figure out
 who the spy is...

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:14.930
Now, shall we take a look at the darkness 
within all our hearts or not?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.930
<b>Pry into the depths of everyone's hearts?</b>

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.930
<b>Pry</b>

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.930
<b>Don't Pry</b>

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.460
How about it, Sempai?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.520
If you want to listen, then I'll tell you.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.780
The story of a murdering loser.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.490
You mentioned that to us before, right?

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.240
What do you mean by that?

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.910
You're right that I know that woman.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:40.940
Her real name is Saotome Ichika.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.000
We were classmates back in high school.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.620
<i>She was a bit of an oddball,</i>

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:51.110
<i>but she was one of the few friends 
I could chat and laugh with.</i>

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.830
She and I were both outsiders in our class.

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:59.400
So we played that off by convincing 
ourselves everyone else was crap.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.500
That the entire world was, too.

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:05.240
We'd talk about that together all the time.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:05.940
But...

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.590
that time we spent together was 
more precious than anything else.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:14.820
<b>Would you like to die with me?</b>

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:14.820
Then one day I got a text from her.

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.280
But I was scared...

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:18.990
Scared...

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:28.270
She threw herself off the Tower, and I...

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.500
I let her die alone.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.680
You call that murder?

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:35.220
That's not your fault at all, Shogo-sempai!

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.380
No.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:40.390
I wouldn't listen to the one request 
from my most treasured friend.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:42.580
I betrayed Ichika.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:47.240
So it's the same thing as killing her myself.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:50.310
Why didn't I go to her back then?!

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:51.940
I regret it more than anything!

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.320
I hated it!

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.080
And I couldn't set foot outside
 my house after that day!

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.900
I shut myself in for a long time after that!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.080
I'm just a hopeless coward!

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:12.730
That was when I found μ's songs 
on the net and got hooked.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.920
They helped only a little,

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.130
but her songs healed my battered heart.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.330
So that's why you came to Mobius?

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:25.830
Yeah. Mobius erased the bitter 
memories just as I wanted.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.120
But then suddenly, Ichika, the woman 
I thought dead, appeared before me

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.850
and forced me to remember everything.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:32.800
It got worse, too.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.750
As if accusing me, she threw 
herself off buildings

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.970
over and over again right in front of me.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.820
It was driving me crazy!

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.130
So that's why you wanted 
to return to reality?

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:49.290
Yeah. So then I started searching 
for other people like me.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.530
And I found you all,

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.480
at the entrance ceremony.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:59.050
You said you've shut yourself in for a long time, 
but how old are you actually?

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.760
30.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:03.640
That's over twice my age!

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.640
Twice?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.100
Uh, no...

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:09.130
Huh? Kotaro-sempai, you're in middle school?

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.490
Which middle school?

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:11.810
Are you making fun of me?!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.310
Stop!

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:14.510
Okay!

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:18.430
So then why don't we have Kotaro-sempai 
tell us about himself next?

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:19.690
You can skip me.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:21.690
Now, don't say that.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.310
I want to know.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:28.200
Why are you so set on being a 
hero of justice, Kotaro-sempai?

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.220
I just...

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.570
My father's a rescue worker, 
and he's really cool.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.760
He's huge and strong.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:41.100
Yet I'm...

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.720
In reality I'm as small as an 
elementary schooler and weak.

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:48.430
Some people just go through 
growth spurts later than others.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.220
That might be true,

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:52.250
but I can't become a rescue 
worker if that's my case!

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.810
My mother and father... both died...

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.070
in an accident.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:04.420
So I was adopted by my relatives.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:08.840
My body and heart are both still so weak.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:14.330
I want to be like my father,
 huge and strong, as soon as possible.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.570
Then I won't be so alone anymore.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.150
Or at least I want to believe that,

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.870
but I'm just not getting any taller.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:28.200
I was wandering through the city 
with those thoughts in my head

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.640
when I heard μ's music playing in a store.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.320
I thought the song was nice.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:37.860
It felt like her song was cheering me on.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.700
Then, before I knew it, I was here.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.580
I do find it fun in here, but...

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.560
No matter how long I stay here in Mobius,

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.020
I'll never become a rescue worker.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.380
I'll never become an adult.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.840
So you want to return to the real world?

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:58.750
But if you go back, you'll be as you were.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.120
My body will be.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:02.860
But not my feelings.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:07.590
Right now, I feel as if I could face 
anything and give it my best shot!

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.310
I kind of understand that feeling, too.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.760
Oh?

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.410
Then next up is...

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.640
Quit asking about others
 and tell us about yourself!

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.480
Me?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.890
There's not that much to talk about.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:25.950
I grew up in an average, ordinary environment
 with no particular talent to speak of.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.660
Just tell us already!

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:28.820
Fine, fine.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:33.080
My parents were ordinary people, 
the kind you could find anywhere.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:37.130
So ever since I was little, I've thought 
I didn't want to end up like them.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.750
And I thought about taking up a
 profession that wasn't ordinary.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.960
When I told my parents

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.480
I wanted to become a composer and 
take the test for a music college,

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:46.550
they gave me conditions.

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:49.480
You can barely play the piano as it is.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.760
Have you given this any serious thought?

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.200
Fine.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.620
In that case, try actually composing 
something. Even if it's just one song.

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:01.480
In the end, I missed my chance.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.580
While I was at it, I realized something.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:07.070
What I sought was just a cool dream,

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.570
and I was still utterly empty inside.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.080
Yet as soon as I came to Mobius,

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.700
I was granted the enticing 
position of "Musician,"

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.790
and great songs came to me easily.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.010
Plus, everyone was caught up
 in listening to them.

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:22.800
Man, that felt great!

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.670
You realized your dream, then.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.410
So why did you decide to 
join the Go-Home Club?

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:28.090
That's just it.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:35.280
When I watched you all struggling to 
regain yourselves and return to reality,

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.560
I realized something.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.520
Ultimately, I'm still empty inside,
 even here in Mobius.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.940
What the heck?!

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.810
Your story really is trivial!

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:47.690
You've never faced hell in or out of Mobius!

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:52.660
Hells are as varied as there are people.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:57.620
Your hell and my hell are different types.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:00.960
He's right.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:03.920
Pardon me.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.350
Are you next, Mifue-chan?

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:11.180
If I recall, you asked μ to 
replace your mother, right?

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:11.760
That's—

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:15.370
No! That wasn't Mifue-chan's intention.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:17.230
μ misunderstood and—

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:17.230
No...

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:23.020
Ultimately the one who hurt my mom both 
in the real world and here in Mobius

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.150
was none other than myself.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.330
Hey, hey, is that Mifue-chan's mama?

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:33.160
My real mother is really fat,

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:37.370
and I've always been scared 
that I'll end up as fat as she is,

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.790
so I ended up being unable 
to eat anything at all,

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.460
and before I knew it, I was hospitalized.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.710
When I arrived at Mobius 
I had a healthy body,

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:50.590
and the mother before me was thin.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:55.850
But my first mother here wouldn't eat 
with me, so she became emaciated.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:01.100
And then I wanted one that 
would eat dinner with me.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.300
So μ quickly granted that wish.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.920
It was my wish.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:11.280
No, μ was just granting my 
own selfish desire, but...

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:15.870
But the first mother I 
had here in Mobius, I...

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:16.830
I...

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:20.290
But, Mifue-chan, you went and 
apologized to your mother, didn't you?!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.290
So it's fine now.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.250
No, it's not fine yet!

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:28.200
I still haven't been able 
to apologize to my mother

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:31.290
suffering in the real world.

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.010
So I want to go back.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.510
I have to go back!

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:36.140
Let's stop this already.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:39.180
A person's trauma isn't something 
to be discussed so casually!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.250
Aren't you one to talk, Naruko-sempai?

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.930
You've been sniffing around the net for info

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.760
on other people and 
uploading it, haven't you?

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.110
Th-That's...

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:47.960
Okay!

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.190
Next is Naruko-sempai!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:56.840
Back in reality I trolled μ's videos.

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.660
That was how I got sucked into Mobius.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:02.000
You love the net that much?

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.840
No, I'd say I actually hate it.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.960
See, my father is a newspaper journalist.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:11.160
So at school everyone teased me

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:14.920
and called me the "media trash daughter."

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:19.640
<b>She's a media trash daughter, 
so I bet her brain's rotten.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:19.640
They wrote awful things about me on the net.
It was incredibly painful.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:23.780
Yet before I knew it, I had started 
posting anonymously, as well.

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.590
The net is a strange place.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:33.000
Soon, it started feeling really 
good to slam out invective posts.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:37.230
After I was at it for a while, 
people started liking my posts,

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.570
<b>All those women throwing pity parties 
for themselves can go to hell.</b>

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.570
and it just made me so happy.

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:41.680
I became full of myself, 
thinking I had finally made friends

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:42.950
that I could talk about anything with.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:44.950
But the truth of it all was

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:49.100
that they were the same group of people 
writing those nasty things about me.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.190
It's ridiculous.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:55.790
Here in Mobius, I actually 
had quite a bit of fun

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:57.930
writing different things 
for the gossiper.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:01.390
So why do you want to go back?

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.910
What Kotaro-sempai said was right.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:07.350
I was sniffing around the gossiper 
for info to upload about others,

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.140
<b>Narukonnu

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.060
constantly worrying about my hits,

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.900
<b>Too chaotic! From Gossiper

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:14.530
but it's not that I really need 
recognition from others for doing that.

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:18.570
So I figured it was about 
time to end the gossiper.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.790
Hold on.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:20.780
Huh?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.000
You don't have to delete it, do you?

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.330
You know...

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.830
There are cool pictures of me on there.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:28.580
What the heck?

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.360
Wait, you're a middle schooler.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.560
Be polite! Use your polite words!

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.710
Shut up!

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:40.330
U-Um, can I go next?

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.510
Go right ahead.

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:43.780
I'm...

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:47.230
not much different in Mobius 
than I am in reality.

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:52.380
I've always been all alone, with no friends.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:51.370
She's always by herself, isn't she?

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:53.310
How isolating. Poor girl.

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:56.400
But I always hoped that someday 
I would make friends with someone

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:00.660
who could understand and sympathize with me.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:05.080
But no one would ask me 
to eat lunch with them.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.540
That's why you did that with Shonen Doll.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:13.370
Komori-kun is the first friend I ever made.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:17.800
So I really... did have fun with him.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:21.900
Also, thanks to that...

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:27.520
Even if I go back, I think 
I can move forward now.

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.220
Move forward, huh?

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.020
That's true.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.060
Oh?

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:36.470
Weren't you the one just saying, 
"yet even that is a fabrication"?

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:38.730
IkeP told me...

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:42.950
That even if this is fake, it's his justice.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.160
That reminds me,

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:49.080
IkeP was always occupied with 
your looks, Izuru-sempai.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.440
These looks are meaningless.

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.710
They only make me feel even more unpleasant.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.140
Back in the real world, my life 
was controlled by my mother,

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:01.270
and I wasn't allowed to do 
anything of my choosing.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:05.620
There wasn't a single thing 
I ever accomplished for myself.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:08.810
Except for one time...

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:17.360
There was one sole action 
I took of my own volition.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:23.820
I carved proof that I was 
my own person into my cheek.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:28.080
Yet μ thought that was a wound.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:31.120
Over and over, it would go 
back to the way it was.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:36.500
But without that scar, 
I can't prove I'm alive!

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:41.840
How a person feels about things 
differs with every individual,

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:46.550
so in the end, it isn't possible 
to fully understand one another.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:47.640
Even so,

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.860
my desire to return to the 
real world is the same.

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:56.580
That fact alone makes it worthwhile 
to work together, in my mind.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.800
I see.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.900
Well, the last one left is Kotono-sempai.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.720
It's a stupid story.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:05.950
Do you all still want to hear it?

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:09.840
Telling us that just makes us
 want to hear it more.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:13.710
If I recall, Ritsu-sempai said something 
about a "Caligula effect."

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.070
Mizuguchi, well done!

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.490
How'd you get it to open?!

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:21.850
Shut up.

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:22.490
Huh?

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.540
I'm through.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.760
This farce of comparing 
tear-jerking revelations

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.640
makes my skin crawl!

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.070
Marie-chan?

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:47.910
Die!

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:29.900
My PC broke when I haven't 
done anything! What do I do?

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:40.890
<b>People constantly seek out the right answer. 
Yet is being right really all that matters?</b>

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:31.370
There's no way you did nothing!

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:33.500
You had to have done something you shouldn't have!

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.430
Do you think people will help you if you blame
the PC and make a fuss? Women like you suck!

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.660
People constantly seek out the right answer.

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.890
Yet is being right really all that matters?
